Gemmont on-board GCC examples
=============================

Keep compiler temporaries in the root home directory instead of the small
/tmp filesystem:

  mkdir -p /root/.gcc-tmp
  export TMPDIR=/root/.gcc-tmp

Compile and run Hello World:

  gcc -O0 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/hello.c -o /root/hello
  /root/hello

Compile and draw VGA color bars:

  gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/vga-colorbars.c -o /root/vga-colorbars
  /root/vga-colorbars

Compile and draw NT35510 LCD color bars:

  gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/lcd-colorbars.c -o /root/lcd-colorbars
  /root/lcd-colorbars

Exercise, capture, and display images on a framebuffer:

  fb-test -f 0
  fbdump -fb /dev/fb0 > /root/fb0.ppm
  FRAMEBUFFER=/dev/fb0 fbv -y /root/image.png

fbv supports PNG, JPEG, and BMP images. fb-test-perf writes benchmark results
to a file, for example "fb-test-perf 0 /root/fb-perf.log". fb-test-rect keeps
drawing random rectangles until it is interrupted.

The examples find the framebuffer names "Xilinx" and "chiplab-lcd", so they do
not depend on whether Linux registers VGA or LCD as /dev/fb0. Pass an explicit
/dev/fbN path to override discovery. With the matching bitstream and Linux,
VGA tty1 accepts local input from the PS/2 keyboard. LCD remains an output-only
framebuffer. Run evtest to inspect keyboard events independently of the console.
